    "legend": "Mastocytosis in the skin in an adult with clinical features of cutaneous mastocytosis (monomorphic maculopapular cutaneous mastocytosis). Immunohistochemistry for tryptase shows a moderate increase in mostly spindle-shaped mast cells (&lt;&lt;32084&gt;&gt;). Only a few neoplastic mast cells show an aberrant expression of CD25 (&lt;&lt;32085&gt;&gt;). A bone marrow biopsy is indicated in this situation, because &gt;&nbsp;90% of adult patients with the preliminary diagnosis of mastocytosis in the skin have systemic mastocytosis, usually indolent systemic mastocytosis.",
