    "title": "<p>Classification and clinical features of cutaneous mastocytosis</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Section authors - not necessary",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 125.9pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"168\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Subtype</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 581.2pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"775\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Clinical features</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 4pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 4pt;\" colspan=\"3\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Maculopapular cutaneous mastocytosis (MPCM) </span></strong><span class=\"Ref-PMID\" style=\"color: #984806; background: #ccc0d9;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{26476479; 26152315}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 1cm; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"38\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&nbsp;</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 97.55pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"130\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Polymorphic MPCM</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 581.2pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"775\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 12pt; text-indent: -12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Usually seen in children</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 12pt; text-indent: -12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Brown, yellow, or pale red papules, plaques, and/or nodules</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 12pt; text-indent: -12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Heterogeneity in number, shape, size, margination, and degree of confluence of the lesions</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 1cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"38\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&nbsp;</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 97.55pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"130\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Monomorphic MPCM</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 581.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"775\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 12pt; text-indent: -12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">The most common subtype in adults; may be present from infancy or childhood</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 12pt; text-indent: -12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Small, round, pigmented macules and papules, ranging from a few scattered lesions to generalized skin involvement with confluent lesions</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 125.9pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"168\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Diffuse cutaneous mastocytosis</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\" style=\"color: #984806; background: #ccc0d9;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{25662299; 22092511}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 581.2pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"775\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 12pt; text-indent: -12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">An extremely rare form of cutaneous mastocytosis occurring in infants</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 12pt; text-indent: -12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Generalized erythroderma, thickened skin, exaggerated folds, and episodic blistering often accompanied by severe systemic symptoms</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 12pt; text-indent: -12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Absence of individual skin lesions</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 125.9pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"168\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Mastocytoma</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\" style=\"color: #984806; background: #ccc0d9;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{26476479; 26525106}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 581.2pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"775\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 12pt; text-indent: -12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">The most frequent type of mastocytosis in infants</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 12pt; text-indent: -12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Mastocytomas are usually solitary lesions, but as many as three lesions are accepted</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 12pt; text-indent: -12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Yellow to brown papules, nodules, or plaques, often with a leathery texture; less frequently, small and pigmented macules</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 12pt; text-indent: -12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Rubbing may cause wheals, blisters, and occasionally flushing and hypotension</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
